## 5. Living Tree etiquette

Parallel agents (Claude, Codex, Gemini) may be editing this repo
concurrently in the same checkout. Do not assume your in-memory view of
files is current.

- **Read before edit, every time.** Even if you "just read it" 30 seconds
  ago.
- **Append-only fields on shared structs.** Don't delete other agents'
  commits.
- **Commit per task, not per run.** Atomic, named, recoverable.
- **Do NOT push during a marbles run** unless explicitly instructed.
  Commit yes; push by operator decision.
- Branch `fix/the-truth-of-findings` is the part-2 working branch.
  Operator decides if part-2 commits stack on it or branch out.

---

## 6. Per-task gates — read every task

Before marking `[x]`, every gate must pass:

| Gate | How |
|---|---|
| Build green | `cargo check --workspace` |
| Clippy green | `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings` |
| Test green | `cargo test -p <crate> <test_name>` (cite the exact test name) |
| Negative check | grep / capability blob / inspection proves bug is provably absent |
| Round-trip e2e | the test drives the wire shape end-to-end where the gap was wire-shape |
| Non-goal respected | the fix does not silently add other surface |

If any gate flickers, **revert and re-think**. Frontier SoTA = a future
auditor reading the test cannot construct a falsifier inside the touched
module.

